 show the  self-reported intensity of ocd symptoms  um that the participants are reporting  using the roon application on a scale of  so from top to bottom we have  participants p3 p4 and p5 and the  colored points are the symbol intensity  readings and the solid line shows the y  box 2 score where higher y box 2 means  more severe ocd  so as i mentioned all three participants  are responders  and the time point at which they became  responders is indicated by these stars  and so p3 and p5 only really recently  reached responder status but p4 who  reached responder status at 30 weeks  after dbs on continues to have pretty  wide variation in symptom severity over  days  and  we find this variation really  interesting because it shows that even  after responder criteria is met  there are still good days and bad days  and symptoms are still fluctuating  and this point acts as further  motivation for developing an adaptive  dbs system that can respond to these  fluctuations and symptoms and  reduce those symptom intensity ratings  in the long term  so each time the participants do a  recording again we ask them to report  their intensity vocabulary symptoms  using that phone application so we can  associate  each recording that they do with a  particular symptom level and this bar  chart summarizes the amount of data and  hours that we've collected  across each symptom intensity level  along with how much data we've collected  during behavioral tasks  during explosion response prevention  therapy and  totally requested over a thousand hours  of lsp across these three participants  and notice that the majority of the data  has been collected um by p4 so this teal  color  this participant has been in the study  the longest and  most of the data  collected by t4 is associated with  symptom intensities of below 3 out of  10.  so even though this participant reported  a wide range of ocd symptoms  after responder status as they showed on  the last slide  they're really only 