sity  for  going across delta band theta band alpha  band beta and gamma bands  for left in the first row  um and right  in the second row bcbi  and i found that bcbs spectral power  shows correlations with ocd symptom  intensity where the correlation between  symptoms and delta-van power showed the  strongest correlation  and theta alpha beta and gamma given  power showed relatively weaker  correlations  so another opportunity to record neural  data during ocd exposures and variable  symptom intensities is during exposure  and response prevention or erp therapy  so the exposure in erp refers to  exposing yourself to the thoughts images  objects and situations that make you  anxious or start your obsessions  whereas the response prevention part of  erp refers to making a choice not to do  a compulsive behavior once the anxiety  or obsessions have been triggered and  all of this is done under the guidance  of therapists  so during the two-month cognitive  behavioral therapy booster phase of our  study  each participant does 13 erp teletherapy  sessions  and  this chart just shows the data streams  available for each one of those sessions  over the two months for p4 and i boxed  out this particular session  of interest that i'll show you a video  clip from on the next slide um here the  exposure was a work  or an image of a word on a finger and  you can see the participant is at home  and the therapist is in the office and  this plot shows heart rate collected  over the whole session and also  throughout the session the participants  have to verbally rate their subjective  units as distressed or substrating  um  and that tracks with the black line so  the video clip i'll show in the next  slide corresponds to the gray shaded  area on that spot  where the  where the introduction of the exposure  happens at the beginning of the clip and  is marked by this vertical black line on  the plot  so the participant that you'll see in  this video has very severe  ocd specific to