ted so i analyzed lsp data in the  same way as before by computing special  power and frequency bands of interest  for each two minute segment around each  symptom intensity rating  and here you can also see some  interesting correlations between studs  and spectral power across frequency  bands  so while delta van power did not show  the strongest correlation here of all  the bands  we did find that the relationship  between delta band power and symptoms  was preserved across planned exposures  during erp  and natural exposures during the sprint  reporting in p4  so the recording platform that i've  described um  enables this type of naturalistic  analysis and  future work will determine the degree of  the consistency of these brain behavior  relationships across patients and their  potential as biomarkers for abs  applications  so to summarize the significance of this  work  for the first time in patients with a  psychiatric disorder we demonstrate the  utility of at home intracranial  recordings which vastly increase the  quantity and ecological validity of the  recorded data we captured over a  thousand hours of lsp data at home  across different symptom levels  and we demonstrate the ability to  measure vcbs spectral power during  natural and planned ocd symptom  provocations at home  using that data we identified delta band  power as a candidate biomarker of high  intensity of ocd symptoms  and continued opportunities for  long-term naturalistic intracranial  electrophysiological recordings  we hope this will propel biomarker  discovery for ocd and other psychiatric  disorders  so next i'll talk about a few emerging  challenges that i think the field faces  so we really need to identify robust  behavioral biomarkers  the utility of self-reported assessments  like intensity of ocd  symptoms are limited as they rely on  patient insight into their own  psychological state which is variable so  we really need enhanced passive  behavioral state monitoring  we also 